dialogue tavernkeeper
  node root marta "Clerk! You've a face like an unfiled form. Sit down and tell me what's written on it."
    > "What's everyone celebrating?" -> marrow
    # One of these fills the second slot, depending on how far along we are.
    > "I need a favour." if not knows_key and not marta_paid -> favour
    > "Bramwick says you have his drawer key." if knows_key and not marta_paid -> key
    > "Thanks again for the key." if marta_paid -> thanks
    > "Bramwick still owes you a game of cards." if seen_iou and marta_paid -> iou
    > "Nothing. Goodnight." -> bye
  node marrow marta "The Marrow sails for the Straits at dawn. Half this room is drinking to a safe voyage. The other half is betting against one, and drinking faster."
    > "Ships keep vanishing out there." -> straits
    > "Who sails on her?" -> crew
    > "Goodnight, Marta." -> bye
  node crew marta "Vane, who could out-stare a gull. Hobb, the bosun, who has more names on his arms than I have on my slate. And a lookout who can spot a lie at two miles and a compliment at none."
    -> crew2
  node crew2 marta "Mind her. She bites, and she's usually right. Those two together are very hard to argue with."
    > "Ships keep vanishing out there." -> straits
    > "I'll mind her. Goodnight." -> bye
  node iou marta "Thirty years he's owed me that game. He'll never pay it. Paying would mean it's over."
    -> iou2
  node iou2 marta "…Don't you dare tell him I said that. I'll water your punch till it's a moral lesson."
    > "Your secret's safe. I'm a civil servant." -> bye
    > "He keeps it in the drawer with the stamp. Right at the front." -> front
  node front marta "Does he. …Get out of my tavern, clerk, before I start liking you."
  node straits marta "Six ships in three years. Five came back drifting, sails set, not so much as a cat aboard. Your father's never came back at all."
    -> straits2
  node straits2 marta "…You're signing on. Don't argue, I can see it. He had that exact look."
    > "Goodnight, Marta." -> bye
  node favour marta "A favour's a debt with better manners. I take mushrooms, gossip and the truth, in that order. Come back with one."
    > "Mushrooms, gossip, truth. In that order. Noted." -> bye
  node key marta "Won it off him at cards. He bet it on a pair of threes, the old fool. It's yours in trade. My broth is as thin as a ledger tonight. Bring me a handful of jet-caps."
    > "I've got some right here." if has mushroom -> traded
      take mushroom
      give drawer_key
      set marta_paid
      note marta_key "Marta won Bramwick's drawer key and would not give it back for nothing. A handful of jet-caps, for the broth, is apparently the rate."
      sound pickup
    > "A handful. Done." if not has mushroom -> bye
    > "Where do I find jet-caps at this hour?" if not has mushroom -> nofungus
  node nofungus marta "Under the pier, mostly. There's a crate on the quay nobody's shifted in years, and they come up thick in the black timber beneath it."
    -> nofungus2
  node nofungus2 marta "You'd want a crowbar. That crate's been nailed down since the last harbourmaster but one."
    > "A crowbar. Noted." -> bye
  node traded marta "Jet-caps! The broth lives. Here's his key. And tell him a pair of threes is not a strategy."
    > "Goodnight, Marta." -> bye
  node thanks marta "Thanks are free, clerk, and I don't deal in free. Pay me in story: whatever's out in those Straits, come back and tell me. I hate an unfinished story."
    > "I will. I'll even get it stamped." -> bye
  node bye marta "Go on. And shut the door behind you; the gossip gets out."
